# Interactive Element Standards (Dialogs, Dropdowns, Popovers)

All dialogs, dropdowns, popovers, modals, and overlay components MUST have solid, opaque backgrounds. Translucent or "see-through" overlays violate design standards and hurt readability.

## Core Principle

**Interactive overlay content must be opaque.** Only the modal backdrop (the dimmed area behind a dialog) may be semi-transparent. No `backdrop-blur` on overlays (causes fuzzy appearance).

## FORBIDDEN Patterns

**NEVER use on interactive content surfaces:**

```tsx
// ❌ FORBIDDEN - Opacity modifiers
bg-background/80  bg-background/90  bg-card/50  bg-white/80  bg-white/90

// ❌ FORBIDDEN - Backdrop blur
backdrop-blur  backdrop-blur-sm  backdrop-blur-md
```

**Correct alternatives:** Use `bg-background` or `bg-card` (no opacity). Use `shadow-lg` for depth instead of blur.

## When Transparency IS Allowed

1. **Modal overlay only** (the dimmed backdrop behind the dialog): `bg-black/40` — no blur.
2. **Marketing navbar only** (glass effect): `bg-background/90 backdrop-blur-md` in marketing components only.
3. **Terminal-style components** (e.g. LivePulse): intentional dark/blur by design.
4. **Subtle hover tints:** `hover:bg-orange-50/50`, `bg-orange-50/30` for unread indicators.

Modal *content* must always be opaque; only the overlay may be semi-transparent.

## Elements That MUST Be Opaque

- Dialogs/Modals — `bg-background`
- Popovers, Dropdowns, Select menus — `bg-card` or `bg-background`
- Search suggestions, Tooltips, Floating controls — `bg-card` with `shadow-lg`
- Navigation headers (platform) — `bg-background` (marketing exception above)

## Dialogs

- **Content:** Use `DialogContent` with default `bg-background` or explicit `bg-background` / `bg-card`. Do NOT override with opacity (`bg-background/95`, etc.).
- **Size:** Use `size` prop: `sm` (425px), `md` (600px), `lg` (800px). Avoid custom `max-w-*` unless needed for wide content; if so, still use `!bg-background` or `bg-background`.
- **Overlay:** Default `bg-black/40` is correct. Do not add `backdrop-blur` to overlay.
- **Cards inside dialogs:** Use solid `bg-card` or semantic tokens. No `bg-white/50`.
- **Wide dialogs:** Use `max-w-[95vw] lg:max-w-7xl`, `min-w-max` for tables, `sticky left-0 bg-background z-10` for first column. Include horizontal `ScrollBar` when needed.
- **z-index:** Dialogs use `z-50`; nested dialogs may use `z-[60]`.

## Dropdowns & Popovers

- **Background:** Use `bg-card` (preferred for elevated surfaces) or `bg-background`. Never opacity modifiers.
- **Required classes:** `bg-card` (or `bg-background`), `border`, `shadow-lg`, `z-50`, `rounded-lg` or `rounded-md`.
- **Border:** Use semantic `border` token only (no `border-slate-200`, etc.).
- **Z-index:** `z-50` for dropdowns, popovers, tooltips; toasts `z-[100]`. No arbitrary `z-[999]`.

Standard pattern:

```tsx
<div className="absolute top-full left-0 right-0 mt-1 bg-card border rounded-lg shadow-lg z-50">
  <DropdownContent />
</div>
```

## Quick Reference

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT
<DialogContent size="md">  // solid by default
<PopoverContent className="bg-card border shadow-lg">
<div className="fixed inset-0 bg-black/40">  // overlay only

// ❌ WRONG
<DialogContent className="bg-background/95">
<div className="bg-card/50 backdrop-blur-sm">
```

## Pre-Commit Check

```bash
rg "bg-(background|card|white)/[0-9]" --type tsx --type ts src/
rg "backdrop-blur" --type tsx --type ts src/
```

Fix or document exceptions. See also `z-index-hierarchy.mdc` for layering.
